A||||2||WisconsinGT||Help! Coolant pipe hanging||||1||
Z||000000||WisconsinGT||12-26-2000||10:35 PM||||Coming home tonight I heard a scraping noise coming from the passengers side. After inspecting the area I noticed that the coolant pipe is hanging on the passengers side. Is there a way to find the areas where the clamps would go to hold the pipe in place? Thanks!||||reg||1
Z||000001||Bob Englert||12-26-2000||11:14 PM||||Just get out and look under the car!  The area where the clamp was should be weathered differently from the rest of the pipe unless it has been missing for a long time.  You should be able to rig something up to support the pipe easily.  <BR><P>------------------<BR>Bob<BR>2 - 87 GT's<BR>85 SE 4 cyl||||reg||1
Z||000002||DavidHenshaw||12-26-2000||11:40 PM||||Yes, er I mean I think there is.<P>I havn't looked under my car and I'm not going to because the weather is bad,...real bad. But looking at the Haynes book, it appears there are four heater brackets as they call them. The two in the front of the car appear to be about 12 inches to the rear of the front edge of the gas tank. The two at the rear appear to be about 4 inches from the rear edge of the gas tank. There is also a "main fuel tank suppoet" in the middle of the tank which appears to provide support for both heater hoses.<P>Of course due to model year changes yours may be a little different from the ones in the book but you get the idea. <P>Dave<P>86 GT||||reg||1
